&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fx9mw6jl70fjxexad35i2.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fx9mw6jl70fjxexad35i2.png" alt="The same chart in a light panel and a dark one, tooltip included." width="799" height="353"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The tooltip is the one part that needs a component. Recharts' default tooltip writes &lt;code&gt;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255)&lt;/code&gt; as an inline style, and we measured it staying white under a dark theme. A tooltip drawn as a Box takes &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; like anything else on the page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The trap in the hand-written version
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hand-written version is a stylesheet like this one:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;:root&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--chart-1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#0284c7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--chart-1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.dark&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--chart-1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#7dd3fc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;When the &lt;code&gt;dark&lt;/code&gt; class is on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, it works. Put it on a section instead (a dark sidebar, a dark card, a preview), and the revenue line stays the light-mode blue. A custom property is resolved where it is declared and inherited as a finished value: &lt;code&gt;--color-revenue&lt;/code&gt; became &lt;code&gt;#0284c7&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;:root&lt;/code&gt;, and redeclaring &lt;code&gt;--chart-1&lt;/code&gt; further down never reaches it. In our probe the dark section's &lt;code&gt;--chart-1&lt;/code&gt; read &lt;code&gt;#7dd3fc&lt;/code&gt; while the line's stroke read &lt;code&gt;rgb(2, 132, 199)&lt;/code&gt;, a light-mode blue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F05iylq1vuqkfplb0ttqk.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F05iylq1vuqkfplb0ttqk.png" alt="A dark section: the chart aliased in :root keeps the light colour, the one in ChartContainer follows." width="800" height="327"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;ChartContainer&lt;/code&gt; declares &lt;code&gt;--color-&amp;lt;series&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; on itself, below whatever theme is around it, so the alias resolves inside the section that chose the theme. Each theme rule is scoped to the subtree that declared it, so a light chart inside a dark page works the same way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Colours of your own
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A list of series takes the palette in order. A record names each series' paint, as anything &lt;code&gt;fill&lt;/code&gt; takes, including a colour with an opacity:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ChartContainer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@box-kite/react/components/chart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Bar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BarChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ResponsiveContainer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;XAxis&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;recharts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;weeks&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;week&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;W1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;started&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;week&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;W2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;started&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;week&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;W3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;started&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;week&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;W4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;started&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Goals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ChartContainer&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;series&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;violet-600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;started&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;violet-600/35&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;vars&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;color-completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;violet-400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;color-started&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;violet-400/35&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResponsiveContainer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"100%"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"100%"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BarChart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;weeks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;XAxis&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"week"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;stroke&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"currentColor"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fontSize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Bar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"completed"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;stackId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"goals"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fill&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"var(--color-completed)"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Bar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dataKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"started"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;stackId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"goals"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fill&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"var(--color-started)"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BarChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResponsiveContainer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ChartContainer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fr6b2zglynfd4h24f2xlo.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fr6b2zglynfd4h24f2xlo.png" alt="Stacked bars in violet, a step lighter in the dark panel." width="800" height="327"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A named paint is the same in both themes, so the dark value is a &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; override, and we measured it winning. A paint the palette does not have (&lt;code&gt;'tael-500'&lt;/code&gt;) declares nothing. In development it warns, with the nearest token: &lt;code&gt;Did you mean "teal-500"?&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The honest limits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Every series still names its variable.&lt;/strong&gt; Recharts takes one string per &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Line&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Area&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, so &lt;code&gt;var(--color-revenue)&lt;/code&gt; is written once per series. A variable nobody declared paints nothing: our grid disappeared until &lt;code&gt;--chart-grid&lt;/code&gt; existed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A canvas chart cannot read a variable.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;ctx.fillStyle = 'var(--chart-1)'&lt;/code&gt; is ignored (we checked), so a chart that draws on a canvas needs the resolved colour from &lt;code&gt;getComputedStyle&lt;/code&gt; and a redraw on every theme change. This approach is for SVG charts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The palette has six slots&lt;/strong&gt;, and a seventh series wraps round to the first colour.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Theme rules need &lt;code&gt;@scope&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Chrome 118, Safari 17.4, Firefox 128 and later. Below that, the light values show.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Recharts' own themes are coming.&lt;/strong&gt; Its experimental provider takes a theme object per chart. Its CSS-variable example uses the same &lt;code&gt;--chart-1&lt;/code&gt; names, declared by hand in a stylesheet. The container is that stylesheet as a prop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/charts" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Charts&lt;/a&gt;: the container, and the small charts that need no library at all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/blog/dark-mode-without-the-flash" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Dark mode without the flash&lt;/a&gt;: the theme the chart follows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;npm install @box-kite/react recharts&lt;/code&gt;, and wrap one chart in &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ChartContainer&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://www.box-kite.dev/blog/charts-that-follow-the-theme/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;box-kite.dev&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt; Box Kite is open source under MIT — if it is useful to you, a star on &lt;a href="https://github.com/box-kite/box-kite" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt; helps other people find it. Install it with &lt;code&gt;npm install @box-kite/react&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Upgrading to Next.js 15 is one line:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gd"&gt;- "next": "14.2.15"
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+ "next": "15.0.3"
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The work is in the files that line affects. Three changes cause most of it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Request APIs are async
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;cookies()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;headers()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;draftMode()&lt;/code&gt; now return promises.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;  import { cookies } from "next/headers";
&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;  export default async function Page() {
&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-   const theme = cookies().get("theme");
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+   const theme = (await cookies()).get("theme");
&lt;/span&gt;    ...
}
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Next.js keeps a temporary synchronous fallback that logs a warning, which is kind for the upgrade and unkind for finding the problem: the code keeps working, and the warning sits in your logs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In route params, the same applies: &lt;code&gt;params&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;searchParams&lt;/code&gt; in pages and layouts are promises too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. &lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt; isn't cached by default
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In 14, &lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt; in a server component was cached unless you opted out. In 15 it isn't cached unless you opt in:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;force-cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Nothing breaks. Some pages that were fast because of a cache you never meant to rely on get slower.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. GET route handlers aren't cached
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Same idea for &lt;code&gt;app/**/route.ts&lt;/code&gt;: a &lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt; handler is dynamic by default now. Add &lt;code&gt;export const dynamic = "force-static"&lt;/code&gt; where you really wanted it cached.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Finding every affected file
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The official codemod handles most of change 1:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx @next/codemod@canary upgrade latest
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then search for what's left, because codemods miss dynamic patterns and helper functions:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;grep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-rnE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"cookies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\(\)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;|headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\(\)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;|draftMode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\(\)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; app src
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;grep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-rn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fetch("&lt;/span&gt; app src | &lt;span class="nb"&gt;grep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-v&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"cache:"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;And run your build and tests before you call it done. &lt;code&gt;next build&lt;/code&gt; catches type errors from the async change if your project is typed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This "the release notes say what changed, but not where it hits &lt;em&gt;your&lt;/em&gt; code" step is the part &lt;a href="https://www.versyka.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Versyka&lt;/a&gt; automates: it reads the release notes against your repository, rewrites the affected calls and runs your checks before and after.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Have you moved to Next.js 15 yet? What broke first?&lt;/p&gt;
